00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:02.800 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  since it was first revealed in 2017  Metro Exodus has emerged as one of the  most eagerly anticipated gaming  prospects of 2019 this third installment  of 4a games distinctive first-person  survival shooter takes place two years  after the events of Metro last light and  promises to take us on a journey beyond  the desolate tunnels of post-apocalyptic  Russia we've experienced so far here are  the reasons we're very excited to  re-enter the ravaged world of the Metro  series after two games spent exploring  Moscow's maze-like Underground system  hero Artyom has now hitched a ride on  Aurora a modified steam train on a  journey to find life beyond the metro  joining him on this quest along the  trans-siberian railway are returning  characters Anna and Miller alongside a  new cast of Spartan Rangers they include  the deceptively named idiot who is  presumably inspired by the protagonist  of the Dostoyevsky novel that shares his  name  now he's made the transition to an  overground transport system Artyom is  going to spend a lot more time exploring  Russia's surface away from the safety of  Aurora he'll have to contend with the  threat of mutants hostile humans natural  environmental dangers and our old friend  radiation poisoning there's also a  persistent day/night cycle so you'll  have to prepare to encounter nocturnal  enemies who will hunt you from the  shadows Metro Exodus hasn't abandoned  the linearity that defined its previous  two installments as it expects from a  game set on a train the story takes  players from location to location on a  fixed route however each location is now  what the game's creators call a sandbox  survival level a vast open space that  can take hours to explore fully you'll  have to scavenge resources survive  against mutants and human enemies and in  a spirit of previous Metro games will  encounter additional quests to distract  you from the task at hand  the method of acquiring weapons in  Exodus has changed significantly  compared to previous metro games new  firearms can now be scavenged from dead  enemies or you can strip their guns for  parts and attachments impressively every  handcrafted weapon is purported to  function in real life such as the  delightfully named bastard gun which  appears to be comprised of parts from a  pipe a bucket some pliers and lots of  imagination  weapons modding has also been expanded  greatly offering five attachments  categories to upgrade and alter  performance namely scope barrel stock  magazine and under barrel the best part  Artyom now has a backpack slung over his  shoulders that contains all the tools  necessary to mod and craft at any time  during his adventure however the world  will not stop around him while he's  tinkering so if you want to prevent  Artyom being swept up by a demon while  he's screwing on a silencer it's  probably best that you first locate a  relatively safe spot gone are the  trading posts of 2033 and last light  which means no more worrying about  footing ammo aside as a currency to  acquire new gear instead there are two  key resources chemicals and materials  the former is used for weapons  maintenance and the latter is essential  for crafting med kits gas masks filters  and ammo for bespoke weapons if you want  to keep the odds in our team's favor  it's going to fade to scavenge every  corner of the world the metro games have  always included an element of choice  with various moments some obvious some  less so impacting on the story's outcome  exodus makes this decision-making a much  more integral part of the experience  giving you freedom to choose how you  tackle situations all guns blazing is  still very much an option but stealthier  approaches can net the same results were  also giving you an opportunity to listen  on other factions conversations and even  if you do ops issues everything in sight  you might find that certain enemies will  surrender giving you dynamic moral  choices do you shoot or do you spare  them you might find that certain spared  foes will come running to your aid as a  critical moment later in the game or  they might just take advantage of your  good nature and have another crack at  killing you  [Music]  as Artyom's horizons expand so -  unfortunately there's the diversity of  mutant enemies eager to tear him apart  joining the returning demons watchman  nozzle is shrimp and lurkers are several  brand new and utterly terrifying  aberrations humanimal czar pack-hunting  mutants who act like rabid apes spiders  are grossly mutated arachnids with an  aversion to light  wolves are well lower wolves but really  hungry and very angry and mutated bears  are just very very very bad news  Metro Exodus runs on forays in-house  engine the very same that powered both  2033 and last lights and one that is  still widely regarded as among the best  in the business  naturally the technology has evolved a  great deal in the 5 years that have  passed since the last game and with  Exodus is much expanded scope the engine  now accommodates a host of new systems  and effects improve lighting superior  textures performance captured facial  animation and dynamic weather systems  all serve to make Exodus the finest  looking Metro to date impressively the  Xbox one X version is promised to  support native 4k resolution with full  HDR  to complement its standout graphics to  Metro Exodus brings photo mode to the  series for the very first time available  from day one photo mode will give  players the chance to document their  adventures from a perspective beyond our  team's headspace and apply their  artistic eye to the twisted beauty of  the Russian wastelands it won't be long  until you can join Artyom and the crew  of the aurora on their epic journey  across post-apocalyptic Russia because  Metro Exodus arrives February 15 2019  [Music]

